  "question": {
    "text": "The correct order in aqueous medium of basic strength in case of methyl substituted amines is:"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>In aqueous medium basic strength is dependent on electron density on nitrogen as well as solvation of cation formed after accepting <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi><mo>+</mo></msup></math>. In&nbsp;protic solvent like water, the order of basic strength is</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi><mo>&#62;</mo><msub><mi>NH</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>This happens beacuse&nbsp;in case of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>NH</mi></math>&nbsp;there will be optimum (+I) and solvation while in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>MeNH</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;has more significant hydration than&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>Me</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">N</mi></math>.</p>"
  }
